-- title:
--   Supersingular places read off injectively from Γ₀(M')-classes
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\kappa_A$ denotes the residue field of a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and for a field $\kappa$ and $N\ge 1$ the field `modularFunctionFieldC κ N` is the intermediate field $\kappa\bigl(j(\mathsf q),\,j(\mathsf q^{N})\bigr)$ of $\kappa$-Laurent series obtained by adjoining `jqModC` and `jqNModC`; `jGeomGen κ N` is the element $j(\mathsf q)$ of it.
--
--   **Arithmetic data at $q$.** A prime $q$ with $5\le q$, a positive integer $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `hA`, namely that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. A finite set $W$ of places of $\kappa_A\bigl(j(\mathsf q),j(\mathsf q^{M'})\bigr)$ over $\kappa_A$ — a place being a valuation subring containing the base field, distinct from the whole field, and a principal ideal ring — is assumed by `hW` to consist exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' κ_A`, the places $w$ with `IsSupersingularPlace q M' κ_A w`; a distinguished element $s\in W$ is part of the data. The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, that is, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field over $\mathbb Q$ is contained in the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^{2}M'$ for $H=\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^{2}M')^{\times}\to(\mathbb Z/q)^{\times}$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Further, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ on $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ with values in $\kappa_A\bigl(j(\mathsf q),j(\mathsf q^{M'})\bigr)$: a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective ring homomorphism `R₀.residue` from it onto that field with kernel its maximal ideal, and a map `R₀.placeMap` on places, subject to the structure's compatibilities (an element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $A$ precisely when its image lies in `integers`; `residue` restricted to $A$ is the residue map of $A$; every non-zero element becomes, after multiplication by a suitable constant, an element of `integers` with non-zero residue; `placeMap` preserves degrees and carries the divisor of an element with non-zero residue to the divisor of its residue). The hypothesis `hR₀` states that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its `R₀.residue`, viewed as a Laurent series over $\kappa_A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **The base field and its valuation ring.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and an element $\pi_0\in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$; write $A_0$ for the valuation subring $A.\mathrm{comap}$ of $k_0$ obtained by pulling $A$ back along $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and $\kappa_0$ for its residue field. The hypotheses on $A_0$ are: `hdvr`, that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; `hunif`, that its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$; `hhens`, that it is a Henselian local ring; `hres`, that $\kappa_0$ is algebraically closed; and `hκ`, that every $a\in A$ is congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to (the image of) some $c\in k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **The auxiliary prime and the function field $K$.** A prime $\ell'$ with $\ell'\ne q$, $3\le\ell'$ and $\ell'\nmid M'$; an element $\xi\in k_0$ that is a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity, together with `hιξ`, the existence of a ring homomorphism $k_0\to\mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$. An intermediate field $K$ of $k_0\subseteq k_0((\mathsf q))$ is fixed with `hK`: $K$ is the $k_0$-base change $\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}$ of the function field of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell')^{2}M'$ for $H=\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M'$, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^{2}M')^{\times}\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell')^{\times}$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell'$; $K$ is an $A_0$-algebra compatibly with the tower $A_0\subseteq k_0\subseteq K$. Finally a non-zero $j\in K$ with `hj`: its Laurent series is the coefficientwise image $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,(\mathrm{jq})$ of the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-function.
--
--   **Functoriality of level structures and of projective models.** The hypothesis `hℓ` states that for every commutative $A_0$-algebra $T$, Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, variable change $C$ and level-$P$ datum $D$ (a quadruple $x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q$ of elements of $T$), `IsLevelPStructure W ℓ' D` implies `IsLevelPStructure (C • W) ℓ' (D.variableChange C)`; `hM` states correspondingly that `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` implies `IsGamma0PowAt (C • W) p k (kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h)`, where $\mathrm{gamma0PowDeg}\,p\,k$ is $1$ if $p^{k}=2$ and $\varphi(p^{k})/2$ otherwise, and `kernelVariableChangeDeg` is the transform $h\mapsto u^{-2d}\,h(u^{2}X+r)$. Next, $\mathcal G$ is a family `GroupLaws A₀` of relative group laws on the projective models of Weierstrass curves with unit discriminant over $A_0$-algebras, with `h𝒢` asserting that each of them admits a points-evaluation (the chord–tangent law) and `h𝒢O` asserting that for each such curve there is a ring homomorphism out of the origin chart ring realising the identity section and killing $x/y$ and $z/y$; $\mathcal T$ is a `LevelTransport A₀ 𝒢 q`, i.e. a functorial transport of raw Drinfeld pairs along $A_0$-algebra maps and variable changes preserving the Drinfeld level-$q$ condition, and `h𝒯` asserts that this transport is compatible with the two sections $P,Q$ after the comparison morphisms of projective models. The hypotheses `hVC` and `hCO` provide, for every $A_0$-algebra $T$ and projective Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, graded ring homomorphisms between homogeneous coordinate rings, satisfying the stated inclusion of irrelevant ideals, realising respectively a variable change $C$ (`IsVariableChangeHom`) and a coefficient change along an $A_0$-algebra map $f$ (`IsCoefficientHom`).
--
--   **The moduli package and its classifying map.** Write $\mathcal R$ for the rigid Weierstrass datum $\mathrm{rigidDataPow}\,A_0\,\ell'\,M'\,q\,h\ell\,hM\,\mathcal G\,\mathcal T$, the product of the $\Gamma_0$-prime-power component for $M'$, the level-$\ell'$ component and the Drinfeld level-$q$ component. The data include an absolute moduli package $P_0$ for $\mathcal R.\mathrm{toLevelModuliDatum}$ (a ring $P_0.B_0$ over $A_0$ with a universal point $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ representing the functor), a point $x_0$ of that datum over $K$ with `hx₀`: its $j$-invariant, as a Laurent series over $k_0$, equals $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,(q\ell')$, the substitution $\mathsf q\mapsto\mathsf q^{q\ell'}$ in $j$; an $A_0$-algebra map $\mathrm{clC}$ from $P_0.B_0$ to the chart algebra $\mathcal C:=\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j=\mathrm{chartAlg}\,A_0\,K\,\{j\}$ (a subalgebra of $K$, the finite chart of the two-chart integral model attached to $j$), and `hclC`: the composite of $\mathrm{clC}$ with $\mathcal C\subseteq K$ is the classifying map $P_0.\mathrm{classify}\,x_0$.
--
--   **The Tate-point pin `hμ`.** There exist a variable change $C$ over $k_0((\mathsf q))$ and a raw point $r$ of $\mathcal R$ over $K$ such that: the class of $r$ is $x_0$; writing $(a,b)$ for $\mathrm{cuspPoint}\,k_0\,(q\ell')$ at the unit determined by $\xi$ and the vector $(1,0)$, the coefficients of $C$ satisfy $C.u\cdot(2a+1/6)=2b+a$, $C.r=-1/12$, $C.s=-1/2$, $C.t=1/24$ (the last three as constant Laurent series); the curve of $r$, pushed to $k_0((\mathsf q))$, equals $C\bullet\mathrm{tateBase}\,k_0\,(q\ell')$, the Tate curve with $\mathsf q\mapsto\mathsf q^{q\ell'}$; for every prime $p\mid M'$, every field $F'$, ring homomorphism $f:k_0\to F'$ and primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta\in F'$, the image of the $\Gamma_0$-component polynomial $r.\mathrm{level}.1\,p$ in $F'((\mathsf q))$ equals the `kernelVariableChangeDeg` transform, for the variable change $C$ pushed along $f$ and the degree $\mathrm{gamma0PowDeg}\,p\,v_p(M')$, of $\prod_{a}\bigl(X-(\mathrm{toricPoint}\,F'\,(q\ell')\,\zeta^{a})_1\bigr)$, the product over $a\in[1,p^{v_p(M')}/2]$ with $p\nmid a$; the level-$\ell'$ datum $r.\mathrm{level}.2.1$ maps to $\bigl(\mathrm{cuspData}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,(q,0)\,(0,-q)\bigr)$ transformed by $C$; and there are $P_x,P_y,Q_x,Q_y\in K$ whose Laurent series are the four coordinates $x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q$ of $\bigl(\mathrm{cuspData}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,(\ell',0)\,(0,-\ell')\bigr)$ transformed by $C$, such that the Drinfeld sections $r.\mathrm{level}.2.2.P$ and $r.\mathrm{level}.2.2.Q$ pass through $(P_x,P_y)$ and $(Q_x,Q_y)$ in the sense of `IsSectionThrough`.
--
--   **Comparison of residue fields.** A ring homomorphism $\theta:\kappa_0\to\kappa_A$ with `hθ`: for every $a\in A_0$, $\theta$ of the residue of $a$ is the residue in $\kappa_A$ of the image of $a$ in $A$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a map
--   $$\Phi:\ \mathrm{ModuliPoint}\,M'\,\kappa_0\ \longrightarrow\ \mathrm{Place}\ \kappa_A\ \bigl(\kappa_A(j(\mathsf q),j(\mathsf q^{M'}))\bigr),$$
--   where the source is the quotient of the type of $\Gamma_0$-pairs over $\kappa_0$ (an elliptic Weierstrass curve together with a point of exact order $M'$) by the relation `Gamma0Pair.Step`, such that $\Phi$ is injective and, in addition, the following holds. Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of the chart algebra $\mathcal C$ and $\psi:\mathcal C\to\kappa_0$ an $A_0$-algebra map whose vanishing set is exactly $y$ (that is, $\psi c=0$ if and only if $c\in y$). Let $x$ be a raw point of $\mathcal R$ over $\kappa_0$ whose class in $\mathcal R.\mathrm{Pt}\,\kappa_0$ is the image of the universal point $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ under $\psi\circ\mathrm{clC}$, and suppose that the affine curve of $x$ has no non-trivial $q$-torsion point over $\kappa_0$ ($q\cdot P=0$ implies $P=0$). Let $g$ be a point of that affine curve satisfying `hg`, whose two clauses are: $g$ has exact order $M'$; and for every prime $p\mid M'$, every $n$ and every non-singular affine point $(x_1,y_1)$ with $n\cdot g=(x_1,y_1)$ and $n\cdot g$ of exact order $p^{v_p(M')}$, the polynomial $x.\mathrm{level}.1\,p$ vanishes at $x_1$. Let finally $r$ be a place of $\kappa_A(j(\mathsf q),j(\mathsf q^{M'}))$ over $\kappa_A$ which is rational (the structure map $\kappa_A\to$ residue field of $r$ is surjective) and whose valuation subring contains $\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,\kappa_A\,M'$, and assume that $r$ reads the point $\psi$ in the following sense: for every Laurent series $gf$ over $\mathbb Q$ lying in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$ such that the corresponding element of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ lies in `R₀.integers`, such that at every place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ one has $\mathrm{ord}_P(gf)\ge 0$ whenever $\mathrm{ord}_P\bigl(j(\mathsf q)\bigr)\ge 0$, and such that $\mathrm{qExpand}\,k_0\,\ell'$ applied to the coefficientwise image of $gf$ lies in $K$ and, as an element of $K$, lies in the chart algebra $\mathcal C$, the two assertions hold that `R₀.residue` of $gf$ belongs to the valuation subring of $r$ and that $\theta$ of the value of $\psi$ on that element of $\mathcal C$ equals $r.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of `R₀.residue` of $gf$. Then
--   $$r=\Phi\bigl([\,(x.\mathrm{curve},\ \text{elliptic by }x.\mathrm{isUnit}\,\Delta,\ g,\ \text{of order }M')\,]\bigr)\qquad\text{and}\qquad r\in\mathrm{ssPlaces}\,q\,M'\,\kappa_A,$$
--   the class being that of the indicated $\Gamma_0$-pair in $\mathrm{ModuliPoint}\,M'\,\kappa_0$.
--
--   This is the supersingular half of the comparison between the special fibre at $q$ of the integral model of the modular curve of level $(q\ell')^{2}M'$ and the moduli of elliptic curves with $\Gamma_0(M')$-structure in characteristic $q$: a place of $\kappa_A(j(\mathsf q),j(\mathsf q^{M'}))$ which reads a given maximal ideal of the chart algebra is identified with the value at the corresponding $\Gamma_0(M')$-class of one fixed injective assignment of places to classes, and is supersingular. It is obtained from the Frobenius-twisted moduli-place form of the same statement and is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.moduliPoint_mk_eq_of_forall_apply_qExpand_eq_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataPow_of_tatePoint`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.moduliPoint_mk_eq_of_forall_apply_qExpand_eq_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataPow_of_tatePoint).
